{"id":994,"date":"2025-12-19T14:30:01","date_gmt":"2025-12-19T13:30:01","guid":{"rendered":"http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/?p=994"},"modified":"2025-12-19T14:30:56","modified_gmt":"2025-12-19T13:30:56","slug":"last-activities-of-the-year","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/2025\/12\/19\/last-activities-of-the-year\/","title":{"rendered":"Last activities of the year"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<p>Now that 2025 is coming to an end, we summarise some of the lastest activities of the members of IMAGINE.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>First of all, Marina Iturrate-Bobes was invited to give a seminar as part of the Q.E.D. series of seminars organised by the Department of Statistics and O.R. and D.M. of the University of Oviedo. The seminar, given on December 15, was entitled <\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-text-align-center\"><em>El arte de medir lo desigual: lo que la asimetr\u00eda nos ense\u00f1a sobre los datos<\/em><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>In this talk, Marina explained her recent research on measures of symmetry.<\/p>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full is-resized\"><img fetchpriority=\"high\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"750\" height=\"1000\" src=\"http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/12\/MarinaQED.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-995\" style=\"width:auto;height:300px\" srcset=\"http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/12\/MarinaQED.jpg 750w, http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/12\/MarinaQED-225x300.jpg 225w, http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/12\/MarinaQED-300x400.jpg 300w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 750px) 100vw, 750px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<p>A couple of weeks earlier, on December 3, Nicol\u00e1s Carrizosa received the Extraordinary Award for the Best Academic Record in the Master\u2019s Degree in Statistics for Data Science at Universidad Carlos III de Madrid.<\/p>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-large is-resized\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"979\" src=\"http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/12\/NicoUC3M-1024x979.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-996\" style=\"width:auto;height:300px\" srcset=\"http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/12\/NicoUC3M-1024x979.jpg 1024w, http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/12\/NicoUC3M-300x287.jpg 300w, http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/12\/NicoUC3M-768x735.jpg 768w, http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/12\/NicoUC3M-1536x1469.jpg 1536w, http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/12\/NicoUC3M-2048x1959.jpg 2048w, http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/12\/NicoUC3M-850x813.jpg 850w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<p>Finally, following our tradition, we organised a meeting of the research group before the Christmas holidays, where we discussed our ongoing research and our plans for the coming year and, more importantly, ended the meeting with a lunch, toasting to a successful year and to continued collaboration in the year ahead.<\/p>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-large is-resized\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"462\" src=\"http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/12\/group-1024x462.jpeg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-997\" style=\"width:500px\" srcset=\"http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/12\/group-1024x462.jpeg 1024w, http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/12\/group-300x135.jpeg 300w, http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/12\/group-768x346.jpeg 768w, http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/12\/group-1536x692.jpeg 1536w, http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/12\/group-850x383.jpeg 850w, http:\/\/imagine-wp.local\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/12\/group.jpeg 2048w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<p><\/p>\n"